WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
An hour has sixty minutes. A quarter of an hour is fifteen minutes.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Here, fifteen minutes have passed since three. We say quarter past three. Past means after.

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Now watch the long hand travel to nine. Forty-five minutes have passed since three.

4
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:38.000
There are fifteen minutes left before four. Count the last three groups: five, ten, fifteen.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:49.000
We say quarter to four. To means before the next hour. The clock still reads three forty-five.

6
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Past looks back to the hour that started. To looks ahead to the next hour.
